<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
		<!-- Deploy wwwroot contents to the app's root, not _content/SpawnDev.WebTorrent/ -->
		<!-- Required for service worker scope — SW must be at app root to intercept all requests -->
		<StaticWebAssetBasePath Condition="$(StaticWebAssetBasePath) == ''">/</StaticWebAssetBasePath>
		<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
		<Version>3.2.2</Version>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>v3.2.2 stable: rollup of rc.1 + rc.2 + rc.3 + the SCTP backpressure polling fix shipped in commit `7fd70c5`. Five SCTP / wire correctness improvements over 3.2.1, no breaking changes. (1) **SCTP backpressure shared-TCS multi-awaiter fix.** `_bufferedAmountLowTcs` is now a shared TCS that every concurrent `Send` references at await time. `OnBufferedAmountLow` completes the shared TCS to release ALL awaiters, then atomically installs a fresh TCS for the next round. Replaces the rc.1 `Interlocked.Exchange`-per-awaiter pattern that orphaned all but the latest concurrent awaiter and timed out at 30s in P2P's 8-chunk pipeline pattern. (2) **`RtcPeer.Send` polling-based wait.** `OnBufferedAmountLow` is best-effort - `DesktopRTCDataChannel`'s 20ms poller only fires on strict above-then-below transitions; rapid SCTP drains miss the transition entirely. `Send` now races the event TCS against a 50ms `Task.Delay` so the next iteration's top-of-loop `BufferedAmount` re-check breaks out when drained. The 120-second wall-clock ceiling covers genuinely-stalled SCTP rather than relying on an event we can't trust. Closes `LargeBuffer_100MB_DispatchedOverRealWebRtc_BitExact` (was failing reliably at 1m37s-7m7s with `TimeoutException` despite `BufferedAmount=0` and `ReadyState=open`; now PASSES in ~5 min). (3) **Duplicate-handshake hardening on Wire.OnHandshake.** Phantom destroyed-wire entries no longer linger in `_wiresByBtPeerId[canonical]`; bridge `RemoveWhere(w => w.Destroyed)` filter on close. Closes `P2PSwarm.TwoTab_PeerDiscovery`'s peerCount-stuck-at-1 regression. (4) **SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.8 stable dep bump** - pulls in Desktop OnBufferedAmountLow now actually firing + browser connection-state polling fallback + opt-in DiagnosticsEnabled. (5) Diagnostic groundwork: `[RtcPeer][BACKPRESSURE-DIAG]` instrumentation. Verified via SpawnDev.ILGPU.P2P real-WebRTC integration tests.</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<EmbedAllSources>true</EmbedAllSources>
		<DebugType>Embedded</DebugType>
		<NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
		<Title>SpawnDev.WebTorrent</Title>
		<Authors>LostBeard</Authors>
		<Description>Pure C# BitTorrent/WebTorrent client. 18 BEPs including BEP 52 v2 (SHA-256 + Merkle + hybrid + pure-v2 end-to-end), real WebRTC P2P (browser + desktop via SpawnDev.RTC), DHT with mutable items (BEP 46 — AI agent communication), web seeds, media streaming with seeking via service worker, OPFS storage. Includes webtorrent-sw.js for COI headers + torrent streaming. No JavaScript dependencies. Runs on desktop (.NET + SIPSorcery) and browser (Blazor WASM + SpawnDev.BlazorJS). 468+ shared test methods running on both browser and desktop runtimes + libtorrent 2.0 external-interop fixtures.</Description>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.WebTorrent</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageIcon>icon-128.png</PackageIcon>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.WebTorrent.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageTags>BitTorrent;WebTorrent;P2P;Torrent;Blazor;WebAssembly;WebRTC;DHT;Streaming;MachineLearning;ModelDelivery;SIPSorcery</PackageTags>
		<NoPackageAnalysis>true</NoPackageAnalysis>
		<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="SpawnDev.WebTorrent.Tests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="SpawnDev.WebTorrent.Demo.Shared" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="Assets\icon-128.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\LICENSE.txt" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.BlazorJS" Version="3.5.6" />
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.AsyncFileSystem" Version="1.2.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.BlazorJS.Cryptography" Version="3.2.0" />
		<!-- SpawnDev.RTC replaces direct SipSorcery dependency - provides cross-platform WebRTC
		     with proven browser-interop SipSorcery fork (SRTP profile fix) bundled inside.
		     PackageReference (not ProjectReference) so CI / GitHub Pages builds work from a
		     standalone SpawnDev.WebTorrent checkout - they don't have the sibling RTC repo.
		     1.1.1 is the minimum version: 1.1.0 declared a dep on public SIPSorcery 10.0.4-pre
		     which doesn't exist on nuget.org; 1.1.1 bundles the fork DLLs inline (ILGPU pattern). -->
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.RTC" Version="1.1.8" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="windows" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="linux" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="macos" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
